## Getting Started

### 1. Enable the Tags Feature

In your `pika-config.ts`:

```typescript
export const siteFeatures: SiteFeatures = {
    tags: {
        enabled: true,
        tagsEnabled: [
            { scope: 'pika', tag: 'chart' },
            { scope: 'pika', tag: 'download' }
        ]
    }
};
```

### 2. Build a Web Component

Create a standard web component:

```javascript
class ProductCard extends HTMLElement {
    constructor() {
        super();
        this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' });
    }
    
    connectedCallback() {
        const data = JSON.parse(this.textContent);
        this.render(data);
    }
    
    render(product) {
        this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `
            <style>
                .card {
                    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
                    border-radius: 8px;
                    padding: 16px;
                    max-width: 320px;
                }
                .product-image {
                    width: 100%;
                    height: 200px;
                    object-fit: cover;
                    border-radius: 4px;
                }
                .product-name {
                    font-size: 18px;
                    font-weight: 600;
                    margin: 12px 0 8px;
                }
                .product-price {
                    font-size: 24px;
                    color: #059669;
                    font-weight: 700;
                }
            </style>
            <div class="card">
                <img class="product-image" 
                     src="${product.imageUrl}" 
                     alt="${product.name}">
                <div class="product-name">${product.name}</div>
                <div class="product-price">$${product.price}</div>
                <button class="add-to-cart">Add to Cart</button>
            </div>
        `;
        
        this.shadowRoot.querySelector('.add-to-cart')
            .addEventListener('click', () => this.addToCart(product));
    }
    
    addToCart(product) {
        // Handle add to cart logic
        console.log('Adding to cart:', product);
    }
}

customElements.define('product-card', ProductCard);
```

### 3. Deploy the Component

Upload to S3 and create a tag definition:

```typescript
{
    tag: 'product-card',
    scope: 'custom',
    usageMode: 'chat-app',
    widget: {
        type: 'web-component',
        webComponent: {
            s3Bucket: 'my-components-bucket',
            s3Key: 'product-card.js',
            encoding: 'gzip'
        }
    },
    renderingContexts: {
        inline: { enabled: true },
        dialog: { enabled: true }
    },
    llmInstructionsMd: `Use the product-card tag to display product information.
    
Example:
<product-card>{"name":"Laptop","price":999.99,"imageUrl":"https://..."}</product-card>`,
    status: 'enabled'
}
```

### 4. Enable in Chat App

```typescript
{
    chatAppId: 'shopping-assistant',
    features: {
        tags: {
            tagsEnabled: [
                { scope: 'custom', tag: 'product-card' }
            ]
        }
    }
}
```

## Advanced Patterns

### AI-Invoked Components

Create components that request structured data from the agent:

```javascript
class DynamicDataTable extends HTMLElement {
    async connectedCallback() {
        const query = this.getAttribute('data-query');
        const schema = this.getAttribute('data-schema');
        
        // Request structured data from agent
        const response = await this.pikaContext.invokeAgent({
            componentAgentInstructionsMd: `Retrieve data for: ${query}`,
            outputSchema: JSON.parse(schema),
            conversationId: this.conversationId
        });
        
        this.renderTable(response.data);
    }
}
```

### Multi-Context Components

Adapt rendering based on display context:

```javascript
connectedCallback() {
    const context = this.getAttribute('pika-context');
    
    switch (context) {
        case 'inline':
            this.renderCompact();
            break;
        case 'dialog':
            this.renderDetailed();
            break;
        case 'spotlight':
            this.renderDashboard();
            break;
        case 'canvas':
            this.renderFullscreen();
            break;
    }
}
```

### State Management

Access conversation state and send messages:

```javascript
class InteractiveWidget extends HTMLElement {
    handleUserAction(action) {
        // Send message to agent
        this.pikaContext.sendMessage(
            `User selected: ${action}`
        );
        
        // Update component state
        this.updateState(action);
    }
}
```

## Best Practices

### Design Principles

{% aside type="tip" title="Progressive Enhancement" %}
Design components to work gracefully across all rendering contexts. Start with inline functionality, then enhance for dialog/spotlight/canvas.
{% /aside %}

{% aside type="tip" title="Streaming-Aware" %}
Always handle all three streaming states (pending, completed, error) for robust user experience during real-time updates.
{% /aside %}

{% aside type="tip" title="Shadow DOM" %}
Use Shadow DOM for style encapsulation to prevent conflicts with application styles and ensure consistent rendering.
{% /aside %}

### Performance

{% aside type="note" title="Minimize Bundle Size" %}
Keep component JavaScript files small. Components are loaded over the network, so minimize dependencies and use code splitting.
{% /aside %}

{% aside type="note" title="Optimize Images" %}
Load images lazily and use appropriate formats (WebP where supported). Consider responsive images for different contexts.
{% /aside %}

{% aside type="note" title="Cache Effectively" %}
Components are cached after first load. Use versioned filenames (e.g., `product-card-v2.js`) for cache busting when updating.
{% /aside %}

### Security

{% aside type="danger" title="Sanitize Inputs" %}
Always sanitize and validate data received from agents. Never use `innerHTML` with unsanitized content.
{% /aside %}

{% aside type="danger" title="CSP Compliance" %}
Ensure components work within Content Security Policy restrictions. Avoid inline scripts and eval().
{% /aside %}

